{{!
    @template mod_booking/bookingoption_description_slotoverview

    Data carrier for the read-only slot availability overview. Renders NO visible markup.

    A user who has used up max_slots_per_user is blocked from the booking button, and with it from
    the slot picker - which is otherwise the only place the option's remaining availability is ever
    shown. This embeds that option's slots so clicking the "Booked" status bar can open them in a
    modal (see mod_booking/slotbooking/slot_overview_modal).

    The list is deliberately NOT rendered here: it is drawn by the same JS renderer the booking
    picker uses (slotbooking/slot_day_renderers renderSlotList), so the day grouping and the row
    markup exist exactly once and the two lists cannot drift apart.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * slotoverviewexist - Whether there is anything to embed. Nothing renders when falsy.
    * slotoverviewoptionid - The option these slots belong to; the trigger is matched to it via the
      data-itemid on .booking-button-area, so several options on one page stay independent.
    * slotoverviewjson - JSON-encoded array of slot DTOs (slot_dto::build_picker_slots()).

    Example context (json):
    {
        "slotoverviewexist": true,
        "slotoverviewoptionid": 5140,
        "slotoverviewjson": "[{\"key\":\"1788357600:1788359400\",\"start\":1788357600,\"end\":1788359400,\"daylabel\":\"Thursday, 3 September 2026\",\"timelabel\":\"9:00 AM - 9:40 AM\",\"status\":\"open\"}]"
    }
}}
{{#slotoverviewexist}}
    <div data-region="slot-overview-source"
         data-optionid="{{slotoverviewoptionid}}"
         data-slots="{{slotoverviewjson}}"
         hidden></div>
    {{#js}}
        require(['mod_booking/slotbooking/slot_overview_modal'], function(module) {
            module.init();
        });
    {{/js}}
{{/slotoverviewexist}}
